@page "/docs/components/theme-switcher"
@using Blaizio.Docs.Examples.ThemeSwitcher
<PageTitle>Theme Switcher - Blaizio</PageTitle>

<div class="typeset typeset-docs space-y-10">
    <header class="docs-page-header space-y-2.5">
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
            <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">Theme Switcher</h1>
            <DocBadges Slug="theme-switcher" />
        </div>
        <p>Three ready-made controls for the light, dark and system preference: a segmented switcher, a radio group that sits inside a menu, and a single toggle button. They all share one theme module, which saves the choice to <code>localStorage</code> and applies it before the first paint through <code>boot.js</code>. Every switcher on the page stays in sync, so changing one updates the rest, and in system mode they follow the OS when it changes. The tokens behind the themes are covered in <a href="docs/theming">Theming</a>.</p>
    </header>

    <UsageBlock Example="typeof(ThemeSwitcherExample)" />

    <ExamplesHeading />

    <Demo Title="Segmented switcher" Description="Shows the saved preference as system, light or dark. Change it next to the switcher in this site's header and watch the two move together."
          Example="typeof(ThemeSwitcherExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Without the system option" Description="Set `ShowSystem` to `false` to hide the follow-the-OS option when you only want an explicit light or dark choice."
          Example="typeof(ThemeSwitcherNoSystemExample)" />

    <Demo Title="In a menu" Description="`BzThemeMenu` is a radio group of menu items, so you can place it inside any dropdown, such as a profile menu."
          Example="typeof(ThemeMenuExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Single toggle" Description="`BzThemeToggle` switches to the opposite of the theme currently on screen. From system mode, the first press lands on an explicit light or dark choice."
          Example="typeof(ThemeToggleExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Single toggle with system" Description="With `ShowSystem`, the button cycles through light, dark and back to following the OS. A monitor icon marks the system step."
          Example="typeof(ThemeToggleSystemExample)" />

</div>
